@startuml UC-A6-keep-the-session-alive-analysis-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-A6 Keep the session alive (analysis: system sequence)
' Analysis level (decision 9): the person, Playground as one box, and Keycloak as an outside system.
' No route, store, port, adapter, token or cookie. Step numbers are the main flow numbers of UC-A6.
' Refusal reasons (session ended, person disabled, already used) are in the main text of UC-A6.
' Not decided yet, so not drawn: Keycloak being unreachable (open in UC-A6, "should the session be kept for a retry?").

actor "Person" as P
participant "Playground" as PG #E6F0FB
participant "Keycloak\n(outside system)" as K #ECECEC

P -> PG : 1 ask for something\n(signed in)
PG -> PG : 2 sign in about\nto run out?
alt still good (> 30 s)
  PG --> P : the answer
else about to run out
  alt a renewal is running
    PG -> PG : 3 wait for it,\nuse its result
  else none running
    PG -> K : 4 renew this sign in
    alt Keycloak refuses
      K --> PG : refused
      PG --> P : sign in again
    else
      K --> PG : 5 a renewed sign in
      PG -> PG : 6 keep it
    end
  end
  PG --> P : 6 the answer
end
@enduml
